  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'By subscribing to the PassthroughLayerResumed event, apps can control
    when they want to display the passthrough layer.


    When the PassthroughLayerResumed
    event is <b><i>not</i></b> used, activating the passthrough layer will result
    in the app showing its content immediately. However, due to the asynchronous
    nature of the start passthrough call and latency, the passthrough textures may
    not be ready yet. This results in a black screen for a short period of time.


    Subscribing
    to the PassthroughLayerResumed event mitigates this problem, as the corresponding
    renderer can be enabled only when the passthrough texture is ready and rendered
    at runtime.


    Toggle the event subscription with the button below and toggle
    the passthough on and off by pressing <color=#FFD200>A</color> or via <color=#FFD200>Thumb
    tap gesture</color>.


    You may need to keep the passthrough layer turned
    off   for a while in order to notice the black screen when turning the layer
    back on.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
